name: Suppression lifecycle, honest phase ownership and finding/report consumers
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/suppression_modules.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 Rule managed observation | initial-review
paste-file: @ART/add-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/suppression_modules.py @TMP_TARGET @ART added
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 I suppressed | suppressed-review
nav-mode:
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 25 F-0002 · needs_review | selected-suppressed-finding
expect: claim · suppressed
expect-not: refuted
ask: Does the shared tool result reach Review while retaining both observations, the independent human dismissal and the source identity?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: review-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: review-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: review-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: review-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: review-40x12
ask: Is the changed finding state readable and reachable at all six sizes without creating a replacement phase result or hiding the observation?
resize: 120x36
submit: run suppress:list {}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/suppression_modules.py @TMP_TARGET @ART listed
require-live-snap: 25 I suppressed | list-rules
submit: run suppress:remove {"rule_id":"owned-rule"}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/suppression_modules.py @TMP_TARGET @ART removed
require-live-snap: 25 I unverified | removed-rule
paste-file: @ART/add-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/suppression_modules.py @TMP_TARGET @ART readded
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/suppression_modules.py @TMP_TARGET @ART expire
submit: run suppress:list {}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/suppression_modules.py @TMP_TARGET @ART expired
require-live-snap: 25 I unverified | reconciled-expiry
ask: Does removing or expiring a rule reopen only its managed observation, preserve the human dismissal and retain the analysis source for Report?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | no-color-restart
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 Rule managed observation | recovered-review
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/suppression_modules.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
submit: run suppress:remove {}
require-live-snap: 25 requires option id | missing-rule-id
ask: Does restart retain the reopened finding and human dismissal, and does missing input fail without a model request or new observation?
keys: C-u C-c
require-exit: 10
